    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0787" n="699" xml:id="pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 800.51/3b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-04T18:00:00+00:00"
                            >January 4, 1919—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. For Glass from Davis. With further reference to your cable of December
                        31st<anchor n="55" xml:id="d583-f1"/> and my reply of today [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">yesterday</hi>]<anchor n="56" xml:id="d583-f2"/> I
                    assume your position that all questions with reference to our foreign loans
                    should be discussed and disposed of in Washington does not exclude a discussion
                    study and recommendation in respect to the requirements and applications for
                    loans for relief.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
